course: dictionary
lesson: 15868
title: Unguarded
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unguarded means not watched or protected by anyone. The word has un- at the start, which means not, and guarded means watched over, so unguarded means not guarded. «The gate to the field was unguarded, so the sheep walked out.» Nobody was there to watch the gate or keep it shut.
explain: You can use unguarded for a place or a thing that nobody is watching. «Never swim in an unguarded pool.» A pool with no lifeguard is dangerous, because nobody is there to keep people safe. Safety signs often warn about unguarded fires and pools for this reason.
explain: Unguarded can also describe a moment, when you are not being careful. «In an unguarded moment, Sam let slip that he had broken the vase.» Sam was not thinking, so he said something he meant to keep secret. Context clues like «let slip» and «secret» tell you what the word means here.
fact: Unguarded means not watched or protected by anyone.
fact: «Unguarded» can describe a place, such as a gate or a pool, or a moment when you are not being careful.
fact: In an unguarded moment, you may say or show something you meant to keep secret.
fact: In sport, an unguarded player or goal is free and open, with no one blocking the way.
fact: Un- means not, so unguarded is the opposite of guarded.
exercise: «The gate was unguarded, so the sheep walked out of the field.» What does unguarded mean here? | Very old and falling down | *Not watched or protected by anyone | Locked with a big key | Painted bright red
exercise: «She let slip her secret in an unguarded moment.» What does unguarded suggest? | Happy and singing loudly | Very careful and quiet | Angry with her friends | *Not careful, so she said something she meant to keep hidden
exercise: Which of these is an unguarded place? | A bank vault with a guard at the door | A school with a teacher on duty | A pool with a lifeguard on the chair | *A field with no one watching over it
test: «The unguarded fire was dangerous because nobody was watching it.» What does unguarded mean? | Very hot | Made of wood | *Not watched by anyone | Put out with water
test: «The striker ran past the defender into an unguarded goal.» What does unguarded mean in this sentence? | Painted in team colours | *Free and open, with no defender blocking it | Full of goals | Locked and closed
exam: Which sentence uses unguarded to mean not careful? | *«He told the secret in an unguarded moment.» | «The gate was locked and guarded all night.» | «The lifeguard watched the unguarded pool.» | «The sheep walked into the unguarded field.»
